---
name: f-tilde-extension-infix
version: 1.0.0
---

# A user-defined `~` extension used infix

`~` is a legal operator name for an extension method, and the parser-combinator
library in `std/parsing/combinators.ssc` is built on it (`~`, `~>`, `<~`).

The F front lexes `~` as the PREFIX bitwise-NOT operator (`opCode` 126 -> 68,
consumed by `parseTilde`), and has no infix reading for it. It therefore accepts
this program and compiles it to something else — no decline, no diagnostic, exit
0, wrong number. The interpreter and the JS lane both call the extension.

This case exists to keep that visible: it is expected RED on v2 until F learns
`~` as an infix extension operator. See `v2/BUGS.md`,
`f-tilde-infix-silently-miscompiled-as-bitwise-not`.

```scalascript
extension (p: Int)
  def ~(q: Int): Int = p * 100 + q

println(3 ~ 4)
println(1 ~ 2)
```
